    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Japanese 31st Division set out with only three weeks' supply of food and ammunition, and its lack of supplies was the decisive factor in the battle.</li><li>Fighting at the Deputy Commissioner's bungalow was so close that the tennis court became a no man's land with grenades thrown between trenches, and the Japanese were not driven from it until a tank was dragged up on 13 May.</li><li>Satō abandoned Naga Village on 31 May against Mutaguchi's orders, and the two commanders blamed each other afterwards.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The garrison's water supply point was on GPT Ridge and was captured by the Japanese on the first day of the siege; a small spring on Garrison Hill could be reached only at night.</p></aside>
    </section>

